WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.141 --> 00:00:02.092
(audience cheering)

00:00:02.092 --> 00:00:04.080
- Possibly coordinate a tiny bit.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:04.913
- Yeah, well, I'm not gonna lie,

00:00:04.913 --> 00:00:05.746
they told me, you know,

00:00:05.746 --> 00:00:07.230
the set's gonna be decorated for Christmas

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:08.100
if you wanna look Christmassy.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.620
And I was like, well, I kind
of already picked this dress,

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.422
but maybe it's kind of that
pastel fifties Christmas.

00:00:12.422 --> 00:00:13.255
- This is Zimmerman.

00:00:13.255 --> 00:00:15.307
- And then I saw you and
I was like, "Oh, stop it.

00:00:15.307 --> 00:00:16.185
"Stop the presses."

00:00:16.185 --> 00:00:17.210
- Do you love,

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.209
did you watch White Christmas growing up?

00:00:19.209 --> 00:00:20.910
- I didn't watch White
Christmas growing up,

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.143
but I mean, it is iconic.
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:00:22.143 --> 00:00:23.520
- And, I mean, that was iconic.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.600
- Oh my gosh, I love that movie so much.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.860
- [Anna] It's beautiful.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.500
- Yeah, what's your Christmas go-to movie?

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.840
- Well, I guess Elf kind
of became the thing,

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.880
but Scrooged and Home Alone,

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:33.900
and you know, those, yeah.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:34.733
- Home Alone, very famous in my house.

00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:36.600
- Classic.
- I have kids.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:37.830
So what holiday traditions

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.360
do you look forward to,
like, with your family?

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.982
- Well, I actually

00:00:40.982 --> 00:00:43.890
just started learning to
make cocktails and stuff.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.540
So like, my new tradition is

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.780
like around Christmas
I'll make French 75's.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:49.613
Do you have French 75's?

00:00:49.613 --> 00:00:51.750
- What the heck, no.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.430
- But when it's Christmastime,

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:54.660
I think they're usually made with gin.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.730
But around Christmastime,
I make them with cognac.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:59.370
And maybe this makes me sound bad,

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:02.055
but I did ask to have some French 75.

00:01:02.055 --> 00:01:03.390
- Oh, I wanna try it.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:04.383
Oh, I didn't know it was happening.

00:01:04.383 --> 00:01:06.480
- They just appeared as if from nowhere.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.220
- No.
(audience clapping)

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.510
Hysterically so,

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:11.490
I was so concentrated on
this performance earlier,

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.020
I didn't even know this
was happening. (laughing)

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:13.853
- I love that.

00:01:13.853 --> 00:01:14.782
- [Kelly] So I love this.
- I love that for us.

00:01:14.782 --> 00:01:15.615
- What is in it?

00:01:15.615 --> 00:01:16.448
I love this for us.

00:01:16.448 --> 00:01:18.495
- It's champagne and cognac
and like some bitters-

00:01:18.495 --> 00:01:19.421
- Merry Christmas.
- Cheers.

00:01:19.421 --> 00:01:20.254
Merry Christmas.

00:01:20.254 --> 00:01:21.098
To your beautiful gown.

00:01:21.098 --> 00:01:22.883
- I feel so classy right now, y'all.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.860
- That smells good.

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:27.030
- Doesn't it feel Christmassy?

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:27.863
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:27.863 --> 00:01:29.098
- I like a mulled wine.

00:01:29.098 --> 00:01:30.961
- I love a mulled wine.
- Me too.

00:01:30.961 --> 00:01:33.660
- I love any excuse to walk
around with a mulled wine.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.860
- Yeah. Casually.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.930
- If there's like a like a farmer's market

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:37.830
with cheese or something.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.237
- Christmas markets.
I love going to those.

00:01:39.237 --> 00:01:40.950
- Oh, suddenly I'm in a Hallmark movie,

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:43.042
and I'm one of those girls
that holds her mug like this.

00:01:43.042 --> 00:01:44.332
(audience laughing)

00:01:44.332 --> 00:01:45.898
- Just cozy like.

00:01:45.898 --> 00:01:49.380
- I have long mittens or
something in this fantasy.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.210
Meanwhile, it's LA and I'm in sweatpants,

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.950
but that's how I feel inside.

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.270
- Do you get into New Year's,

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:56.760
or are you like an at
home, like this is a long-

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:58.590
- New Year's is so much pressure, right?

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.906
It's that same kind of
like Christmas anxiety.

00:02:00.906 --> 00:02:04.080
It feels like such, like forced fun.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:06.000
I usually just kind of hide out.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:06.833
- You feel like you have to have

00:02:06.833 --> 00:02:07.850
the greatest time in the world.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:09.210
- Greatest time of your
life, or you failed,

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:10.350
and you suck as a person.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.134
- I'm such an extremist in general,

00:02:12.134 --> 00:02:14.670
and I either, yeah, I go all out.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.950
Like I'm trying to win some
award for New Year's Eve.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:20.190
Or I do nothing, and
I'm on PJs with my fam.

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:23.130
- Well this year a friend invited me to

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:26.078
a party that's like a theme party.

00:02:26.078 --> 00:02:28.500
And so I was like, oh,
I'll do a little costume.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.080
But then it turns into like
a competition in my mind.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.578
- Oh, who's gonna the cooler costume.

00:02:32.578 --> 00:02:33.720
- Like who's gonna have
the coolest costume.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:37.500
So now I'm like on Amazon
and Etsy every five seconds

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.037
going like, okay, if I
pair like the red glove

00:02:40.037 --> 00:02:41.422
with the gold rings.

00:02:41.422 --> 00:02:43.770
And now it's like become a whole.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.480
It's like the Christmas mantle thing.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:47.850
Where like I don't have
like much of a creative-

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:48.683
- [Kelly] So this is the thing.

00:02:48.683 --> 00:02:49.920
- Like visual outlet.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.900
So now I'm like hyper-focused

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.610
on having the best costume at this party

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.590
where nobody needs me
to have a good costume.

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:56.490
(audience laughing)

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.939
- Let's talk about the new
movie that is so intense.

00:02:58.939 --> 00:03:00.960
It's called Alice, Darling.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.900
And this role is pretty personal.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:04.770
I was saying it, I was like,

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:06.360
I remember us having a conversation.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.253
I don't know if it was the
last time you were here?

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.390
- I know. I was like, is
this okay to bring up?

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:10.470
But I was like-
- Totally for me.

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:13.180
Like, I mean, it's wild
because the first time

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:16.260
that I was on your show, whatever it was,

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:17.410
a year and a half ago, or whatever.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:18.750
And it was a couple months before

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:19.950
I went and made this movie.

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:22.500
And I was so excited to be on your show,

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:23.580
and you were such an incredible host.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:25.401
And then during the commercial breaks

00:03:25.401 --> 00:03:27.930
somebody said something that like

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.672
I ended up talking about what I was

00:03:29.672 --> 00:03:30.990
going through at the time.

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:31.920
- We were both going through

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.110
like kind of devastating breakups.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:34.943
- Yes.
- Yeah.

00:03:36.423 --> 00:03:38.370
Not a thing you wanna have
in common with someone.

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:39.454
But yet we did.

00:03:39.454 --> 00:03:40.343
- But hey, we bonded.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.784
And I realized like at that point

00:03:43.784 --> 00:03:46.922
I was just coming out of it
and I was realizing like,

00:03:46.922 --> 00:03:50.760
it was so hard for me to

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:52.500
like not talk about it.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.670
And I'd spent so long-

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:54.503
- 'Cause you're still working it out.

00:03:54.503 --> 00:03:55.680
- Not talking about it.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:58.260
That then it was like
the floods gates opened

00:03:58.260 --> 00:03:59.093
and suddenly I was like,

00:03:59.093 --> 00:04:00.630
oh, I'm trauma dumping on Kelly Clarkson.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:01.560
Oh God.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:02.790
- That's what everyone does.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:03.623
I mean, I do that too.

00:04:03.623 --> 00:04:04.860
It's like you don't know where to put it.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.180
And so that's why my girlfriends

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.590
probably heard me say the same things

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:08.580
over and over and over again.

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:11.040
Through tears, and laughing hysterically.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.555
And just, you know, back and forth.

00:04:12.555 --> 00:04:13.830
- Yeah.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:14.907
No, but I-
- It's hard.

00:04:14.907 --> 00:04:16.620
It's like your way of working through it.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:17.453
- Totally.

00:04:17.453 --> 00:04:18.360
And it was one of those
funny things where we were

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.560
kind of joking about, like,

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.080
we were like really da da da da.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:23.310
Like talking, comparing notes, whatever.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:25.350
And then like we were
coming back from commercial,

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:27.120
and it was like, all right,
performance of a lifetime.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.320
Nothing's wrong. Here we go.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:30.098
We're on TV. It's all fine.

00:04:30.098 --> 00:04:31.107
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:31.107 --> 00:04:33.370
- And yeah, so the movie is about

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:36.300
psychological abuse and emotional abuse.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:39.150
And really the power of friendship

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:41.520
in the way that you can get through things

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:43.243
if you have the right
people in your corner.

00:04:43.243 --> 00:04:46.770
And, I mean, I know that
that's how I got out,

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:49.353
and how I like started my recovery.

00:04:50.804 --> 00:04:52.696
And yeah, the movie was

00:04:52.696 --> 00:04:54.557
like so personal that

00:04:54.557 --> 00:04:56.896
there was a point where I was like, oh,

00:04:56.896 --> 00:05:00.480
I don't know if this is too
soon to be doing this role.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:01.770
- To like bring you back.

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:02.603
- Yeah.

00:05:02.603 --> 00:05:05.040
But I had I think like six months

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:08.400
between getting the script
and starting production.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.190
So I had some time to
kind of grapple with it.

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:12.660
But, it was really cathartic.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:13.493
- Do you find that it helps though?

00:05:13.493 --> 00:05:15.270
Because I wrote a whole record,

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:16.680
and it's like I wanted to get out of it,

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:17.850
but I also wanted to get it out.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.110
And it just wasn't all out.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:19.994
And I just needed,

00:05:19.994 --> 00:05:21.633
I just wanted to almost like,

00:05:21.633 --> 00:05:23.190
in order to cross the bridge,

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:25.620
it's like you have to handle
all the things on the bridge.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:26.453
You know?
- Yeah.

00:05:26.453 --> 00:05:27.780
No, I think,

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:30.330
it's funny because I I don't
wanna suggest that like,

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.250
oh, there's a scene where
I cried about this thing

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:33.600
and I'm healed now.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:36.360
But the process of making the movie

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:39.288
was really healing, because like-

00:05:39.288 --> 00:05:40.253
- You're getting to experience
through a character.

00:05:40.253 --> 00:05:42.180
- It was so fascinating.

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:45.730
There was a point where I,

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:47.917
early on the director was like,

00:05:47.917 --> 00:05:49.747
"Oh, can we just grab
like a a moment of you

00:05:49.747 --> 00:05:51.007
"where you're like lying in the hammock,

00:05:51.007 --> 00:05:52.050
"and maybe you're reading a book."

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:53.257
And without thinking, I was like,

00:05:53.257 --> 00:05:55.417
"Oh, I would absolutely
go out to the hammock

00:05:55.417 --> 00:05:56.467
"with the intention of reading a book,

00:05:56.467 --> 00:05:59.127
"but Alice wouldn't be able to read it."

00:05:59.127 --> 00:06:01.260
Like, you're stuck in fight or flight,

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.930
and your brain is on this
loop and you can't think.

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.220
And you might try to read that book,

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:06.489
but you'll get like a paragraph in.

00:06:06.489 --> 00:06:07.980
So I think I would just be like

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:09.300
staring into the middle distance,

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.027
unable to to do anything but try

00:06:11.027 --> 00:06:14.499
to figure out how to fix
what was going on in my life.

00:06:14.499 --> 00:06:18.000
And it was easier for me to look at Alice

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.828
and go, "Oh, that's really messed up."

00:06:19.828 --> 00:06:23.400
Because it was so much harder
to look at the fact that

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:24.956
I know that from my own experience,

00:06:24.956 --> 00:06:26.873
and that's really messed up.

00:06:26.873 --> 00:06:29.550
So it was a really fascinating process.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:30.960
- I love that this movie addresses that.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:32.389
I love that your character addresses that.

00:06:32.389 --> 00:06:34.920
I love that it addresses
the whole kind of process.

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:36.390
And then it ends up, you know,

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:38.070
your friends pull you, not pull you out,

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:38.970
you have to pull yourself out.

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:41.100
But having that, you know,

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.450
I just learned this thing from somebody,

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:43.560
but having that kitchen table.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:45.409
Having your kitchen table
of friends around that,

00:06:45.409 --> 00:06:46.800
that's your support system.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.532
That's like, it's important.

00:06:48.532 --> 00:06:52.200
- No, and the friendships
in the movie are flawed,

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:53.370
because the people are flawed,

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:55.440
because we're all human flawed.

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:58.410
But it's really beautiful the way

00:06:58.410 --> 00:06:59.874
that they just keep showing up.

00:06:59.874 --> 00:07:02.394
And I think that's one of
the hardest things to do

00:07:02.394 --> 00:07:05.280
when someone that you love is suffering,

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:08.192
is to just keep showing up
even when they're not okay.

00:07:08.192 --> 00:07:10.470
And to not invade and control and fix.

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:11.716
- Not try and fix it.
- Yes.

00:07:11.716 --> 00:07:13.560
And like it's, yeah,

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:15.330
such a radical act of love

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:16.777
to just be like, "You're not okay,

00:07:16.777 --> 00:07:19.474
"but I'm still available
to you and I'm still here."

00:07:19.474 --> 00:07:21.994
And that was like really

00:07:21.994 --> 00:07:24.807
one of the things that got me

00:07:24.807 --> 00:07:26.340
through the last couple of years.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:29.700
- It's a project you're gonna
probably remember forever.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:31.170
Just because of the
personal experience as well.

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:33.784
But when Anna was doing
press for Alice, Darling,

00:07:33.784 --> 00:07:36.248
I have to, there is no
segue, it's just funny.

00:07:36.248 --> 00:07:37.463
- But that's okay.

00:07:37.463 --> 00:07:39.182
We're talking about a
serious thing, but it's okay.

00:07:39.182 --> 00:07:41.340
You're wearing glitter, it's great.

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:42.720
- I'm wearing glitter and sparkles

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:44.379
while talking about emotional abuse.

00:07:44.379 --> 00:07:45.570
- As we should.

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:47.700
- I think that we have
a clip of this though.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:48.540
We have to see this.

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:49.620
Okay. Show it.

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:50.580
- [Woman] Never know when you're gonna

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:51.704
get stuck in an elevator.

00:07:51.704 --> 00:07:53.886
- [Anna] Did you say open up the hatch?

00:07:53.886 --> 00:07:56.795
- [Woman] Everybody watch your head.

00:07:56.795 --> 00:07:58.000
I can't believe this is happening.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.143
Are you (beep) kidding me.

00:08:00.143 --> 00:08:01.580
- [Man] Come on. We got you.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:02.700
- [Anna] It's a good thing

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:05.130
I'm not wearing a short skirt today.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:06.330
- I know.

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:07.680
- It was my worst nightmare.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:09.000
You're obviously in an elevator.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:10.650
- Yeah. So we got stuck in an elevator.

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:11.857
This is the first day of press

00:08:11.857 --> 00:08:15.075
at the Toronto Film
Festival for Alice, Darling.

00:08:15.075 --> 00:08:17.760
Yeah. A bunch of us got
stuck in an elevator.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:19.380
And at first like the elevator jolts,

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:21.277
and you're like, you all make
a little joke about like,

00:08:21.277 --> 00:08:23.927
"Can you imagine if we got
trapped in this elevator?"

00:08:25.436 --> 00:08:27.420
And then it was like I was in Die Hard.

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:28.487
I was like, they pull you.

00:08:28.487 --> 00:08:29.530
'Cause I thought, you know-

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:31.140
- Great Christmas film.

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:32.700
- Even though they call
the fire department,

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:33.533
you're like, oh,

00:08:33.533 --> 00:08:35.280
they're gonna like pry open
the doors or something.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:37.440
But we were actually stuck between floors,

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:38.640
and we had to do the thing of like

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:40.470
getting pulled up through the hatch.

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:41.700
It was very exciting.

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:44.141
It was like the most action
star thing I've ever done.

00:08:44.141 --> 00:08:47.275
- [Kelly] Is this before
or after your press day?

00:08:47.275 --> 00:08:48.960
- This is before.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.820
This was like at the beginning of the day.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:52.500
So I sat down to start doing

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:54.510
the first press junket for Alice, Darling.

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:56.673
And every journalist that
came in to interview me,

00:08:56.673 --> 00:08:57.906
I was like, "Oh, I'm so sorry I'm late.

00:08:57.906 --> 00:08:59.880
"I was just stuck in this elevator."

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:00.713
And da da da.

00:09:00.713 --> 00:09:01.747
And all of them just thought like,

00:09:01.747 --> 00:09:02.580
"Oh, Anna's funny."

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:04.241
So she's doing like a bit.

00:09:04.241 --> 00:09:06.571
And the more that I was like,
"No, you don't understand."

00:09:06.571 --> 00:09:07.733
- And then that drives you insane.

00:09:07.733 --> 00:09:10.290
- We just now got pulled
out of the ceiling

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:12.870
of the thing of the
elevator by firefighters.

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:14.400
And they're like, "She is so funny."

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:16.320
(audience laughing)

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:17.970
She is really committed to this bit.

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:19.020
She is too funny.

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:21.180
- You can just say you're late, girl.

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:22.419
Oh my God.

00:09:22.419 --> 00:09:23.851
That's my worst nightmare, by the way.

00:09:23.851 --> 00:09:25.447
And I always make that joke when I go in,

00:09:25.447 --> 00:09:27.681
just so it won't happen.

00:09:27.681 --> 00:09:29.160
That's what I literally do,

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:31.049
to psych, to just trip up the universe.

00:09:31.049 --> 00:09:32.970
Like, "Oh, wouldn't it
be funny if it happened."

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:33.803
And then it didn't.

00:09:33.803 --> 00:09:34.636
- Well, it didn't work for me.

00:09:34.636 --> 00:09:35.610
- Yeah, it didn't work for you.

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:36.960
I shall not say it anymore.

